{
  "problem": "Read N (0 <= N <= 20000), a target, and N signed 32-bit integers. Count index triples i < j < k whose values sum to the target, counting each index triple once. Print the exact count followed by a newline. Use an algorithm asymptotically better than O(N^3) so the maximum input size is practical; a sorted two-pointer O(N^2) method is suitable. Use sufficiently wide integer types for sums and the count.",
  "problem_contract": {
    "description": "Count all index triples i < j < k with values[i] + values[j] + values[k] == target. Do not count permutations of the same indices more than once. Must meet the N <= 20,000 constraint using an algorithm asymptotically better than O(N^3).",
    "operand_type": "64-bit signed integers",
    "sum_type": "64-bit signed integer count",
    "input_range": "0 <= N <= 20,000; values and target fit in signed 32-bit integer",
    "output_rule": "Print the exact triplet count as a decimal integer followed by a newline."
  },
  "time_limit_s": 2,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
